  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multi-profile with avgpool aggregation is clearly superior (config_002: 0.591 vs config_003: 0.519), and adding ResNet50 image features via concat fusion yielded our best result (config_018: 0.619 vs RNA-only config_002: 0.591). However, image-only ResNet50 was very weak (config_010: 0.208), raising the question of whether the modest 3-point multimodal gain is limited by the image encoder quality. Question: Does a stronger, ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L encoder unlock substantially more signal from the image modality in the multimodal setting? Why this is the best next experiment: It directly extends our best configuration (multimodal, multi-profile, avgpool, concat) along the most impactful untested axis—image encoder capacity. A large gain would confirm the image modality has real complementary signal and justify further image-encoder investment; a small gain would indicate the image contribution is inherently limited, redirecting effort toward RNA encoder improvements (scvi/scgpt). This single experiment resolves a critical design uncertainty that would shape all subsequent choices."
}

